([65]).** If δ(G) ≥ 2 and G ≠ C<sub>n</sub>, then dim(G) ≤ 2c(G) − 1 and edim(G) ≤ 2c(G) − 1.\\n\\nIn [65], Sedlar and Škrekovski showed that Conjecture 2 holds for graphs with minimum degree at least 3. They also showed that if Conjecture 2 holds for all 2-connected graphs, then it holds for all graphs G with δ(G) ≥ 2. Recently, Lu at al. [53] addressed Conjecture 2 and showed that dim(G) ≤ 2c(G) + 1 when G has minimum degree at least 2.\\n\\n**Conjecture 3 ([64]).** Let G be a connected graph. If G ≠ C<sub>n</sub>, then mdim(G) ≤ ℓ(G) + 2c(G).\\n\\nConjecture 3 is known to hold for trees [42], cacti and 3-connected graphs [64], and balanced theta graphs [63]. The following conjecture on distance-edge-monitoring sets was also posed recently.\\n\\n**Conjecture 4 ([30,31]).** For any graph G, dem(G) ≤ c(G) + 1.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSedlar–Škrekovski mixed metric-dimension conjecture | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/383319/sedlar-skrekovski-mixed-metric-dimension-conjecture)\\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Sedlar–Škrekovski mixed metric-dimension conjecture\\n\\nFor every connected graph $G$G that is not a cycle, the mixed metric dimension satisfies $\\\\operatorname{mdim}(G)\\\\leq \\\\ell(G)+2c(G)$mdim(G)≤ℓ(G)+2 c(G), where $\\\\ell(G)$ℓ(G) is the number of leaves and $c(G)$c(G) is the cyclomatic number.\\n\\n# Sedlar–Škrekovski mixed metric-dimension conjecture\\n\\nFor every connected graph $G$G that is not a cycle, the mixed metric dimension satisfies $\\\\operatorname{mdim}(G)\\\\leq \\\\ell(G)+2c(G)$mdim(G)≤ℓ(G)+2 c(G), where $\\\\ell(G)$ℓ(G) is the number of leaves and $c(G)$c(G) is the cyclomatic number. Moreover, equality holds if and only if $G$G is either a cactus graph in which every cycle has precisely one vertex of degree at least $3$3, or a balanced $\\\\Theta$Θ-graph.\\n\\nReferences\\n\\n## Primary source\\n\\narXiv\\n\\n## Additional references\\n\\n  * Graphs att